  cpp_errors.pcpp - C++ integration compliance: C++ mistakes are clang's

  A mistake in mixed C++ is reported by clang (ZB0016), at the .pcpp line
  and column it is written on (BNF.md sec 10, DESIGN.md sec 5): in a C++
  declaration and inside a cpp("...") expression alike. This file is
  built, never run; with one error per build (the CLI) only the first is
  reported, the editor and the tester show both.

  How to check, from repo\bin:
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_errors.pcpp
    pcpp res\tests\cpp_errors.pcpp -t x86_64-linux-gnu
  Each marked line reports that code; nothing else is reported.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe cpp_errors;

int Broken() { return GMissing; } // ERROR ZB0016@23: use of undeclared identifier 'GMissing'

begin
  println("{}", cpp("GAlsoMissing + 1")); // ERROR ZB0016@22: use of undeclared identifier 'GAlsoMissing'
end.
